WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.069
-My next guest
is a talented performer

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.438
and "New York Times"
best-selling author.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:08.374
He has a new Audible Original
called "Revelation:

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.977
Connecting with the Sacred
in Everyday Life,"

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.745
which is available
starting Thursday,

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:14.780
exclusively on Audible.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.117
Here is Russell Brand!

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.785
-Oh, my goodness.

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:22.021
That's the real deal.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.723
Look at --
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.392
That is a stud right there.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:28.227
Russell Brand,
it's so great to see you.

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:30.497
Thank you for doing this.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:34.133
-It's an honor to come on your
television program with you

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.069
to discuss this "Revelation"
book that I've written,

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:38.838
Audible Original.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:39.973
-Yeah.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.075
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:45.578
It feels like you have to
legally say "Audible Original."

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.380
-No, no, that's just
naturally how I speak.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.248
These are just my natural
speech rhythms.

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:50.550
I say, "Audible Original."

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.084
For me, it's a natural
thing to say.

00:00:52.084 --> 00:00:54.320
What is a book?
What is the point in a book?

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.188
What have they ever done for us?

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.324
-[ Laughing ] What is going on?
I want to talk --

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:01.261
-See that in the background?
That's satire.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:04.564
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.899
-Oh, I missed you, buddy.
I want to talk --

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:09.536
-They're all Audible Originals,
that little lot.

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.571
-[ Laughing ] That's not true.
That's not true.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.572
These are --
I want to talk about this.

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:16.743
This is a big deal.
"Revelation," Audible Original.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.612
The original vision
you had for this

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.414
is very different
than what you ended up with.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.682
Can you talk about

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:26.586
what the original plan
for "Revelation" was?

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:30.122
-Yeah, my plan was to travel
'round the world,

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:33.459
and while doing that,
I was going to meet people,

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:36.028
learn the secrets of the sacred,

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:38.597
so that I could realize
and actualize myself.

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:41.467
Along the way, I was planning
to do a lot of handshaking

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:46.305
and exchange spores orally
with wise people.

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:50.343
Then there was a little, old
event called coronavirus-19

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.511
that really put a spanner
in the works, Jimmy.

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:56.049
So I was reduced to sort of
sitting on my own meditating

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.150
and trying to contact
the divine that way.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.552
-How would you describe this?

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:02.789
How would you describe
"Revelation?"

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.224
-"Revelation" is --
And this is a tough one, really,

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:07.493
because let's face it --
I'm on your TV show

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.329
to promote an Audible Original.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:13.166
It's that there is no sanctuary,
no peace, no glory,

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.401
no connection
unless we journey within --

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.937
that the reason the world is
fragmenting, fracturing,

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:21.674
falling apart is because we've
become lost in an illusion.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.610
[ Chuckling ] That's why I've
come on your television program

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.812
to promote it to you.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:30.316
-Throughout "Revelation," you
talk a lot about the pandemic.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:34.419
And like me, you have
two young daughters at home.

00:02:34.419 --> 00:02:36.555
What was lockdown like

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:41.427
with two kids
under the age of 5?

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:45.397
-Well, Jimmy, that was
a revelation in itself.

00:02:45.397 --> 00:02:47.767
It's because --

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.870
What it's like
to have two young daughters

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:55.208
is like experiencing
extremely powerful love

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:59.779
laced with devastating rudeness.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.214
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:05.618
-By you or your daughters?
I'm sorry, just to clarify.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:09.822
-Well, I really, really try
my best to remain level-headed.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:13.860
You know, like, say if you want
to leave a place, and they say,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.928
"I'm not leaving this place!
I'm not leaving!"

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:18.931
And you go, "It's okay for you
to want to stay at the party,

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:21.633
and I hear that you want
to stay at the party,

00:03:21.633 --> 00:03:25.404
but we do have to leave."

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:28.107
What my daughter said is,
"You're a [bleep]"

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.475
-Oh, hey, wait, wait --

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.210
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.745
-What in the world?

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.849
-My dog's trying to get in.
Let him in.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:40.053
-Can your dog do any tricks,
Russell?

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.687
-[ Chuckles ] Yeah, kind of.

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:43.022
Come in here.
-[ Whistling ]

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.524
-Not new ones. Bear, come in.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.425
-Oh, sorry.
-[ Whistles ]

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:48.527
Bear is the name of your dog?

00:03:48.527 --> 00:03:50.329
-Yeah, there he is, look.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:52.298
Here he is.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.534
-Aww. Bear.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.135
Bear, Bear --
-Isn't he magnificent?

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.837
-Sit, Bear, sit.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.204
Oh, look at that!

00:03:59.204 --> 00:04:02.274
That's amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:06.178
Russell, if your parenting's
anything like your dog training,

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:08.214
you have nothing to worry about,
my friend.

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:10.783
Um, Russell, I wanted to ask you
a quick thing,

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.285
if you don't mind.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.453
I think I'd like to,
if you don't mind,

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:17.289
teach me a breathing exercise.
Is that okay?

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:19.291
So anyone at home would like
to learn how to relax.

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:21.861
-Okay, this is a very simple
breathing exercise

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.929
that was taught to me
by a great teacher.

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:26.099
Her name is Biet Simkin.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:30.135
Sit your ass down on your heels,

00:04:30.135 --> 00:04:32.738
if you would be so kind.

00:04:32.738 --> 00:04:35.040
-Oh, to do this.
-This breathing exercise,

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.478
you could experience
a glimpse of the divine.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:39.912
I think you could experience

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:43.316
the temporary suspension
of your ego.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:46.853
-Are you just making me "sit,"
like Bear? I feel like Bear.

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:48.487
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.487 --> 00:04:49.955
-When you inhale, Jim,

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:52.358
you got to inhale very,
very deeply into your belly,

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:55.394
as if you're pregnant
with oxygen itself, okay?

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:56.929
This is what an inhale
would look like.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.030
[ Inhales sharply ]

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:00.800
With the chin pointing skyward,
okay?

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.302
So you inhale like this,
filling the belly.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.970
And when you exhale,
you fall forward

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.373
[Exhales sharply] like that,
and you collapse into it, okay?

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.041
So we inhale like this.
[ Inhales sharply ]

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:10.743
And you'll exhale --
[ Exhales sharply ]

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.177
Collapse forward and relax.

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:14.680
-I think I felt it.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.782
-No, Jimmy, that's not it.

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:18.751
This is -- That's not it.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:21.654
This is -- Allow me to take you
to the next level.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.756
So, you do three inhalations
like that,

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.090
where you fill your belly.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.860
[ Breathing sharply ]

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.862
And on the fourth inhalation,

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:33.065
you stand on your knees
like that, okay? You thrust up.

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:35.601
Sorry for that shot.
I'm so sorry for that shot.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.869
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:40.072
Oh, it's like --

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:42.241
Like Elvis the Presley,
Elvis the pelvis.

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.543
It's all been undone.
It's coming reverse.

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:45.945
Let me move back a bit.
-Yep.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:48.180
-Alright, Jim, so,
the fourth one is the big one.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.248
You got to really pull it in.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.917
So, inhale.
[ Inhales sharply ]

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.885
Push the belly out. Exhale.

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:54.020
Inhale. [ Inhales sharply ]

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.422
Push the belly out.
Exhale. Inhale.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:57.923
[ Inhales sharply ]
Push the belly out.

00:05:57.923 --> 00:06:01.094
And on this one, stand up
on the knees, the inhale.

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:02.694
Hold it. Pump the belly out.

00:06:02.694 --> 00:06:04.897
Pump the belly out. Now exhale.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:06.499
[ Exhales sharply ]

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:09.402
-Alright, thank you.
Oh, my gosh.

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:13.805
-Jim, you should feel
a lot closer to God.

00:06:13.805 --> 00:06:15.541
-Russell Brand, everyone.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.376
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:18.577
-I hope you feel healed.

00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:20.345
-Russell Brand, everyone.

00:06:20.345 --> 00:06:24.283
"Revelation: Connecting with
the Sacred in Everyday Life"

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:26.052
comes to Audible on Thursday.

